id:                     E400
trigger_tool:           conan|bun|node|shadow-ci
phase:                  build|packaging|testing|verification
error_signature:        Check failed.*__errno_location|Signal 5|Executable not found.*bun|WebAssembly.*undefined|Permission denied.*bin/ai|exit 126

severity:               2
category:               ohos, conan, testing, node-runtime, package-cache
match_keywords:         ai-cli, Node.js, Bun 1.3.9, V8 JIT, jitless, Signal 5, WebAssembly, OpenH264, Conan package cache, cross-UID, launcher, shadow CI
title:                  Node.js CLI on HarmonyOS: JITless/WASM capability boundary and cross-UID package-cache consumer validation

root_cause:             On the tested HarmonyOS armv8 image, Node.js v24.13.0 exits
                        with Signal 5 and `Check failed: 12 == (*__errno_location())`
                        before ai-cli business JavaScript runs. Narrow V8 optimization
                        flags do not avoid the failure; `--jitless` does. The same
                        runtime mode makes `typeof WebAssembly` undefined, so a
                        prebuilt Node CLI containing OpenH264 WASM has a capability
                        trade-off rather than a lossless runtime workaround. Separately,
                        Shadow CI Conan package cache materializes the launcher with
                        a different UID and mode 0750, so direct execution by the SSH
                        test UID returns exit 126 even when the recipe requested 0755.

affected_scope:         Node.js 22+ CLI packages with prebuilt JavaScript bundles and
                        optional or required WebAssembly assets, built as Conan binary
                        packages and consumed from a cross-UID HarmonyOS package cache.

verification_cmd:       Checkout the upstream source commit and run `bun test` with
                        Bun 1.3.9 and the lockfile; on OHOS run normal Node and V8
                        narrowing probes, then `--jitless` version/help plus
                        `typeof WebAssembly`; run the packaged launcher through the
                        target shell from the Conan package folder and run a negative
                        test after removing package bin/lib/include paths.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           capability-matrix-and-package-folder-consumer-test
rec_description:        Keep Linux on normal JIT. On OHOS, fail closed for unsupported
                        architectures, use `--jitless` only as a target-specific
                        fallback after recording the normal-JIT failure, and explicitly
                        probe WebAssembly before claiming multimedia support. For
                        cache materialized launchers, execute the real package-folder
                        launcher through `/system/bin/sh` on OHOS, retain direct
                        execution on Linux, and pair the positive consumer test with
                        a destructive package-content negative test.
rec_command:            bun test; node --version; node --jitless --version; node --jitless -e "console.log(typeof WebAssembly)"; /system/bin/sh test.sh
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               target-conditional-node-launcher-and-consumer-test

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      runtime-capability-restriction
fallback_description:   If WebAssembly is required by a command, mark that command
                        unsupported on the tested JITless runtime instead of claiming
                        full CLI functionality; do not silently substitute a Linux
                        binary or a different Node target.
fallback_command:
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:

forbid_1_pattern:       node.*--jitless.*WebAssembly|WebAssembly.*supported|cases_run.*0.*pass|bun.*test.*skip
forbid_1_reason:        JITless can disable WebAssembly and an unrun upstream suite
                        cannot be reported as passing; text-only smoke is not complete
                        multimedia validation.
forbid_1_consequence:   Users receive a false capability claim or reviewers accept an
                        incomplete upstream test result.

forbid_2_pattern:       chmod.*0755|/system/bin/sh.*source|test.*package.*bin|PATH.*bun
forbid_2_reason:        chmod does not override cross-UID cache materialization, the
                        test must execute the real package launcher rather than source
                        files, and Bun child-process tests need a reproducible PATH.
forbid_2_consequence:   A consumer test can pass the wrong artifact, fail only due to
                        runner setup, or hide a package cache permission boundary.

principles: P005, P010, P013
doc_file: doc/E400.md
last_updated:           2026-08-20
source_event:           ai-cli 0.4.2 PR #5837 reviewer requested knowledge draft and upstream Bun test evidence
source_pr: !5837

metrics_success_count:  1
metrics_fail_count:     0
